User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dever-labs/angular-micro-frontend/commits/0fb85ef710a7a94bd05063420ed26f6f1c160500/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:03:59Z","email":"casper.elkrog@dever.dk","name":"czprz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:03:59Z","email":"casper.elkrog@dever.dk","name":"czprz"},"message":"feat: introduce @app/mfe-state-model — state contract pattern\n\nThe broker (@dever-labs/ngx-mfe-broker) is now fully generic.\nApp-specific state knowledge lives in a separate contract package.\n\n@app/mfe-state-model:\n- AppState interface: defines the shape of all shared MFE state\n- APP_STATE_KEYS: typed key constants derived from AppState (no magic strings)\n- APP_INITIAL_STATE: default values — passed to shell''s provideNgxMfeBroker()\n- injectAppState(): typed accessor returning WritableSignals per AppState field\n\nPattern:\n- Shell calls provideNgxMfeBroker({ initialState: APP_INITIAL_STATE }) once\n- Remote MFEs just call injectAppState() — no setup needed\n- For multi-repo: publish @app/mfe-state-model to npm as a shared contract\n- For monorepo: local file: reference is sufficient\n\nRemoves mfe-state.keys.ts from @dever-labs/ngx-mfe-broker — it was app-specific.\nShell builds clean after migration.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac4918b57099bb3240785a062e3643feeb815723","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dever-labs/angular-micro-frontend/git/trees/ac4918b57099bb3240785a062e3643feeb815723"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dever-labs/angular-micro-frontend/git/commits/0fb85ef710a7a94bd05063420ed26f6f1c160500","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57328905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/events{/privacy}","followers