rris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/89e8d38236bd204c36f34edaa85a0b0f60f6aa42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:34:30Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:34:30Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"chore(deps): take facet_generate 0.20\n\n0.20 fixes the Kotlin generator qualifying a type in a sibling namespace\nwith the current module''s name rather than the root package\n(redbadger/facet-generate#121). Any core that groups its types into more\nthan one namespace — the normal shape once an app has several features —\nemitted Kotlin that did not compile.\n\nSource-compatible here: the breaking change is a new public field on\n`CodeGeneratorConfig`, and this crate builds facet configs through\n`Config::builder`, never as a struct literal. `facet` stays at =0.46.5\nand `facet-generate-attrs` at 0.18.","tree":{"sha":"ab881e288815ef204ab23962e5cc9c0187aad96a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/ab881e288815ef204ab23962e5cc9c0187aad96a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/89e8d38236bd204c36f34edaa85a0b0f60f6aa42","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/89e8d38236bd204c36f34edaa85a0b0f60f6aa42","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDg5ZThkMzgyMzZiZDIwNGMzNmYzNGVkYWE4NWEwYjBmNjBmNmFhNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2","sha":"9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2"}],"sha":"89e8d38236bd204c36f34edaa85a0b0f60f6aa42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/89e8d38236bd204c36f34edaa85a0b0f60f6aa42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:51:46Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:51:58Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"docs: point the stable book at 0.20.0 and correct release.md\n\n`docs/STABLE_REF` moves to `crux_core-v0.20.0`, now that the tag exists and the\ncrates are on crates.io. It had been left at `crux_http-v0.19.0` because the\npages workflow refuses a ref that names no tag, so it could not move until the\nrelease was cut.\n\n`release.md` pointed at `scripts/cargo_publish.fish` and `scripts/tag.fish`, and\nthere is no `scripts/` directory at all — both references were dead. Those steps\nare now written out as the commands they replace, matching what the 0.20.0\nrelease actually did:\n\n- tagging via `jj tag set` / `jj git push --tag`, noting these are lightweight\n  tags, as every previous release used and as the pages workflow expects\n- publishing one crate at a time, with the caveat that a capability crate cannot\n  be `--dry-run` before `crux_core` is on the index, because it requires the exact\n  `crux_core` version that does not exist there yet\n- creating the GitHub release with `--verify-tag`, so it attaches to the pushed\n  tag rather than creating a new one, and setting `--latest` explicitly, since\n  GitHub awards it to whichever release was created most recently\n\nIt also gains the two steps it never had — waiting for CI on the merge commit,\nand updating `docs/STABLE_REF` — drops `crux_platform` from the capability list\nsince that crate is gone, fixes the duplicated numbering, and records that a\nminor bump is the breaking bump pre-1.0.\n\nSeparately, `docs/VERSIONING.md` documented the pages sanity check as\n`git rev-parse --verify \"$(cat docs/STABLE_REF)^{tag}\"`. The workflow actually\nuses `^{commit}` (pages.yaml:37), and `^{tag}` would have failed against every\ntag this repo has ever cut, all of which are lightweight.","tree":{"sha":"149e88b6f003f51d512ed5c37cf8b0283a7f9a20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/149e88b6f003f51d512ed5c37cf8b0283a7f9a20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDljYTAzZjM1NDVjN2I2OTViZTBkMWU0OWQxYmRhOTI1YzQzZjA0ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f","sha":"a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f"}],"sha":"9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9ca03f3545c7b695be0d1e49d1bda925c43f04e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:18:21Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:18:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #571 from redbadger/readme-single-source\n\ndocs: make the root README canonical and share it with crux_core","tree":{"sha":"eaa26b865fe3fd3b1af574e1842b80778f1c51e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/eaa26b865fe3fd3b1af574e1842b80778f1c51e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f","verification":{"payload":"tree eaa26b865fe3fd3b1af574e1842b80778f1c51e5\nparent ffa0888d742c34af0e142e4a818ce651c3195a94\nparent 98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e\nauthor Stuart Harris <stuart.harris@red-badger.com> 1786112301 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786112301 +0100\n\nMerge pull request #571 from redbadger/readme-single-source\n\ndocs: make the root README canonical and share it with crux_core\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdektCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+vkQAFkAzHoFc24Olm7N8tQl3wBv\nWx88lvAGUonIaopCA58nC1pZgqVWuxaAPy2iUJsANcn3xcsNxmJ6NiREWtzPLlcn\nNMvALuwjYN5xMsM8b0o9sXhmWT2S0hmCrqjpmPV1VY9iTvFBC5v7Id+A0TJjfLlT\nsdv2g5wVm8RmhltR9AHpItUaL4TUr82/xii/Xcj/koUhXJSsnx7nUZygJvrdvpsr\noQVovD7ddVI6WAjP7wWRaSvw8xnova9TYY1Elrzw+CWdY9M1G6Tre6Ettn0/I6er\nbKl2c/4sOkFj81PzsVsbzrWpdCss0BDFKkO4SOpYeLBu/5BN571MmXFTYYk4ATVH\nqKsbzl+MONM1GppP0TqXUm1RqgwmWuQiSR6njv2fAFHUyZTbKinwsYB68ECVJnOz\n43rWK7oRv0VEe1Gy+rORmMuwtbv0RAqT927q6JkQTKEbPRieTi+znRgNLLzr5HV/\nEahtrpAAMXaUjA2t9wjYqPGl/kfzeTKbl1KhNlg/SfA6lrvbAPbs3G5CjsL3Keg/\nkLF86aiobr4ZdGebed3xdAoVWX5BXT+6AyG5ekn0agn7Xnpqhqj+Wlycei/LXseF\nQBZpsQa25OVTktxVMhlh7CO7/swYMrm4kC7b5MWl8gNBhNBWcrdHATYVVT1bvdZO\ns7tIFS+QX9w56bC60EWm\n=3+wk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T14:35:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKGEzZDEyNTZlY2FkNmE0M2ZiYjZhYmM0NWI5NzEyNGU5MjBmNzJiNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/ffa0888d742c34af0e142e4a818ce651c3195a94","sha":"ffa0888d742c34af0e142e4a818ce651c3195a94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/ffa0888d742c34af0e142e4a818ce651c3195a94"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e","sha":"98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e"}],"sha":"a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/a3d1256ecad6a43fbb6abc45b97124e920f72b4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:31:11Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:09:43Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"docs: make the root README canonical and share it with crux_core\n\nThe GitHub landing page and the crates.io landing page for `crux_core` were two\nfiles saying nearly the same thing, and they had drifted in *both* directions.\n\nThe root was ahead on: BoltFFI named as the FFI generator; iOS/Android described\nas BoltFFI packaging rather than Java Native Access; no stale Surf reference for\n`crux_http`; the live `part-2/effects.html` book link; all six examples listed;\na Talks & Articles section; and prose fixes (\"side-effect-free\", \"pre-1.0\",\n\"an `id`\", \"Zulip sponsors\").\n\n`crux_core`''s was ahead on the Bridge API: the root still presented\n`process_event`/`handle_response` as \"the core API interface\", with a `uuid`\nrather than an `EffectId`, and still told the reader the shell calls\n`process_event` and replies to `handle_response`.\n\n`crux_core`''s also carried two dead book links — `guide/effects.html` and\n`guide/capability_apis.html`. `docs/src/guide/` now holds only two http pages,\nand `capability_apis` no longer exists in the book at all.\n\nSo the root README takes the better half of each, and there is now only one\nREADME: `crux_core` points at it with `readme = \"../README.md\"`, which cargo\ncopies into the package at publish time (verified by extracting the built\n`.crate` — a regular 14,760-byte `README.md`).\n\nA symlink would also have worked for cargo, but not for everyone checking the\nrepo out: Git for Windows leaves `core.symlinks=false` unless the user has\nDeveloper Mode or admin rights, and materialises the link as a plain file\ncontaining the text `../README.md`. Nothing in the build reads the README, so\nWindows CI would have stayed green while Windows contributors saw a twelve-byte\nstub — and a publish from such a checkout would have shipped it. The manifest\npath has no such failure mode.\n\nWhat made them two files in the first place was link bases: repo-relative links\nresolve on GitHub but not on crates.io. Every link and image in the shared file\nis therefore absolute. The cost is that links point at `master` rather than the\nbranch being viewed, which for a page that is mostly prose and external links is\na fair trade for making drift impossible.\n\nSince the README no longer lives inside the crate, the two SVGs it used move out\nof `crux_core`: `architecture.svg` was byte-identical to\n`docs/src/architecture.svg` and is simply dropped, and `crux_logo.svg` moves to\n`docs/src/images/`. Nothing else referenced either. That takes the published\ncrate from 765 KiB to 475 KiB, and from 306 KiB to 109 KiB compressed.\n\nVerified: `cargo package -p crux_core` including the verify step, every\nrepo-pointing URL in the README resolves to a path that exists, clippy gate,\nfmt, 246 tests.","tree":{"sha":"eaa26b865fe3fd3b1af574e1842b80778f1c51e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/eaa26b865fe3fd3b1af574e1842b80778f1c51e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDk4ZmNiNzQzNTM4NWJiM2NjODVhODQzMTI3ZWIwZmE5NmFiZjM0M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e","sha":"9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e"}],"sha":"98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/98fcb7435385bb3cc85a843127eb0fa96abf343e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T10:19:47Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:03:41Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"chore(release): refresh crux_core docs, drop unused deps, add categories\n\nRelease hygiene for the 0.20.0 crates, all of it invisible to the compiler\nand none of it touching library behaviour.\n\n**The crate docs no longer teach UniFFI.** The \"Integrating with a Shell\"\nsection of `crux_core`''s crate-level rustdoc — the docs.rs landing page — still\nshowed `uniffi_macros::include_scaffolding!`, a hand-written `hello.udl`,\n`lazy_static!`, `Core::new::<Capabilities>()` (that turbofish went several\nreleases ago) and the `Bridge` methods deprecated in 0.17.0. It now shows the\n`update`/`resolve`/`view` trio wrapped for BoltFFI, matching\n`examples/counter/shared/src/ffi.rs`, with the `#[boltffi::export]` and typegen\nsteps described alongside.\n\nThe block was `rust,ignore`, which is how it rotted unnoticed; it is now a real\ndoctest, so the next signature change breaks the build instead of the reader.\n\nThe README carried the same staleness — `process_event`/`handle_response` as\n\"the core API interface\", FFI \"provided by Mozilla''s UniFFI ... or wasm-pack\",\nserde-generate as the typegen story, and an `App::update` signature still\ntaking `_caps: &Capabilities`. The `Capability` API it warned was \"being\ndeprecated\" is in fact gone: no `CapabilityContext` remains in the crate.\n`App::Effect`''s doc comment pointed at the removed `Effect` derive rather than\n`#[effect]`.\n\n**`crux_http` drops `anyhow` and `pin-project-lite`** — no reference to either\nanywhere in the crate (cargo-machete). `serde_bytes`, which machete also flags\nin `crux_http` and `crux_kv`, is a false positive: it is used through\n`#[serde(with = \"serde_bytes\")]`.\n\n**All five published crates gain `categories`**, alongside the `keywords` they\nalready share from `[workspace.package]`; they are currently uncategorised on\ncrates.io.\n\nVerified: `cargo fmt --check`, clippy clean across the workspace with\n`--all-features --all-targets`, 242 tests, doctests including the new one,\n`cargo doc --all-features` under `-D warnings`, `cargo package -p crux_core`,\n`just check-versions`, and a `cargo check` of the four example workspaces that\ndepend on `crux_http`.","tree":{"sha":"89c97a4c94e42d00c61e4d6aac47204dba32ea1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/89c97a4c94e42d00c61e4d6aac47204dba32ea1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDliOTU4MTZlNTJiM2MxOGEwYzY2NDVlNTQyOWFlOWY3MmQ4M2UwMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536","sha":"8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536"}],"sha":"9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9b95816e52b3c18a0c6645e5429ae9f72d83e01e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T18:11:49Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:03:41Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"chore(deps): use published facet_generate 0.19 and facet-generate-attrs 0.18\n\nBoth are on crates.io now (redbadger/facet-generate#117 released as\nfacet-generate-v0.19.0), so the temporary path deps to the sibling checkout go\naway and the workspace resolves them from the registry with a checksum. This\nis what makes the release publishable: cargo publish cannot resolve a path\ndependency outside the workspace.\n\nAlso corrects the crux_core 0.20.0 changelog entry, which was written before\nthe facet work and still claimed facet_generate 0.18. It requires 0.19 and\nfacet =0.46.5, and now says so, along with a note that anything else in the\ntree depending on facet has to agree — the failure mode is a confusing\n`Facet<''_> is not satisfied` rather than a version conflict.","tree":{"sha":"6d50eca9d9200fd626577a2c019c310709d4c15d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/6d50eca9d9200fd626577a2c019c310709d4c15d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDhjNjQ0NDdiMGM3NDY4M2JmMmFiM2RmMmJiYzI5MGM3ZWYzNWE1MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c","sha":"da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c"}],"sha":"8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/8c64447b0c74683bf2ab3df2bbc290c7ef35a536"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:35:30Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:03:41Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"build(just): hold the facet pins to lib.just in check-versions\n\ncheck-versions already policed BoltFFI and Binaryen, whose versions are spread\nacross manifests, package.json files, CI and the book. facet has exactly the\nsame problem and was not covered: it is pinned in ten places — the workspace\nmanifest, all six example shared crates, the book''s shell chapter, and two\nlines of renovate.json.\n\nfacet is the worst of the three to get wrong. A partial bump does not surface\nas a version conflict: cargo resolves two facet_core versions quite happily,\nand the failure arrives as `RenderOperation: Facet<''_> is not satisfied` from\nwhichever crate landed on the wrong side — which reads like a broken derive,\nnot a version mismatch. That is exactly how it failed while preparing this\nrelease.\n\nAdds a lower bound on the number of pins found as well as checking each one, so\nthat renaming or moving a pin site fails loudly instead of silently shrinking\nwhat gets verified. Both failure modes are verified: drifting one example''s pin\nnames that file, and removing a pin site trips the count guard.","tree":{"sha":"71112425835f4b1fc509337d621822e08c4bad48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/71112425835f4b1fc509337d621822e08c4bad48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKGRhMTJhMTU5NDYwMWUxOWZkZmE3NmZmYWE1MDM0MjM1OTc4YjE0NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f","sha":"5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f"}],"sha":"da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/da12a1594601e19fdfa76ffaa5034235978b146c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:33:38Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:03:41Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"chore(deps)!: facet 0.46.5, facet_generate 0.19 (path deps for now)\n\nMoves every facet pin together: the workspace manifest, all six example\nshared crates, the book''s shell chapter, and the renovate rule. They have to\nmove as one — bumping only some of them puts two facet_core versions in the\ngraph and fails with `RenderOperation: Facet<''_> is not satisfied`, because a\ncrux type deriving Facet from one facet is then registered through crux_core\ncompiled against another.\n\nfacet 0.44 -> 0.46.5 needs no source changes. The delta is additive and lands\nin parts of facet we do not use: facet-core gained list pop/swap, `char` and\n`()` now advertise Clone in their TypeOps, and facet-reflect grew its `poke`\nmodule. facet-macros is byte-identical, so there are no new derive attributes.\nThe Shape/Field/Variant surface facet_generate reads is unchanged, and\ngenerated Swift, Kotlin, C# and TypeScript are byte-for-byte identical — 75\nfiles verified against the facet 0.44 output.\n\nTEMPORARY: facet_generate 0.19.0 and facet-generate-attrs 0.18.0 are not\npublished yet (redbadger/facet-generate#117), so they are wired up as path\ndeps to the sibling checkout to let `just ci` run. Both must be swapped back\nto registry versions before publishing — `cargo publish` cannot resolve a\npath dependency outside the workspace. The Cargo.toml comment says so at the\ncall site.","tree":{"sha":"8ffeafb05c7d8199add20d6279ade3d29b65f8e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/8ffeafb05c7d8199add20d6279ade3d29b65f8e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDViMmE4NjQyMTAzNzIzOGFkMTY2YTA3ZDhlZWUxNWU2YTQ2MTAwMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/02d7afaf63e750e3cc60dc9293d6a50e6138629c","sha":"02d7afaf63e750e3cc60dc9293d6a50e6138629c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/02d7afaf63e750e3cc60dc9293d6a50e6138629c"}],"sha":"5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/5b2a86421037238ad166a07d8eee15e6a461002f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/02d7afaf63e750e3cc60dc9293d6a50e6138629c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T15:26:13Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:03:41Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"chore(release): crux_core 0.20.0, crux_http 0.20.0, crux_kv 0.14.0, crux_time 0.18.0, crux_macros 0.10.1\n\ncrux_http 0.20.0 is the substantive release: HttpError::Http now means only\na server rejection, with two new variants for the cases that were not one,\nand it carries the rejected response''s headers. Its CHANGELOG entry was\nalready drafted under [Unreleased] and is now dated.\n\ncrux_core 0.20.0 exists to move its facet_generate requirement from 0.17 to\n0.18, under the facet_typegen feature. That requirement lives in\n[workspace.dependencies], so it does not show up in a diff of crux_core/\nitself, but it is consumer-visible: 0.19.0 requires facet_generate ^0.17, so\na project wanting facet_generate 0.18 of its own would resolve two\nincompatible copies of it. The library source is otherwise identical to\n0.19.0 apart from doc comments.\n\ncrux_kv 0.14.0 and crux_time 0.18.0 have no source changes at all. They move\nbecause each capability crate requires a specific crux_core minor: leaving one\non crux_core 0.19 alongside another on 0.20 would pull two incompatible\ncrux_core versions into one tree, with two distinct Effect and Operation\ntrait sets.\n\ncrux_macros 0.10.1 carries the fix for registering a generic operation type\nunder typegen, and stays a patch on purpose. Both crux_core 0.19.0 and 0.20.0\nrequire crux_macros ^0.10.0, so 0.10.1 reaches everyone on either — including\npeople not yet ready for crux_core 0.20.0. A 0.11.0 would reach neither\nwithout a further crux_core release. Nothing in this crate''s manifest is\nconsumer-visible either way: its only workspace dependencies are\ndev-dependencies.","tree":{"sha":"052ef47326ce310b40103d83968120999fc114fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/052ef47326ce310b40103d83968120999fc114fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/02d7afaf63e750e3cc60dc9293d6a50e6138629c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/event