"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/ffa0888d742c34af0e142e4a818ce651c3195a94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/f678527d42048d893eabd07d0e757f0f0bd4792b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T10:45:04Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T12:46:21Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"refactor(core)!: rename effects::EffectId to ParkedEffectId\n\nTwo public types were called `EffectId`, and they are not interchangeable:\n\n  `crux_core::bridge::EffectId` is `pub struct EffectId(pub u32)` — the `id` on\n  `Request`, and the value every shell passes back on the serialized lane.\n\n  `crux_core::effects::EffectId<T>` is an opaque `u64` phantom-typed by\n  `Op::Output`, packing a slab index and a generation, handed out by the\n  `Parked` lane for custom FFI.\n\nA shell wiring up both lanes needs both in scope, so one has to be aliased —\nwhich is exactly what `tests/effect_router_prototype.rs` had to do, importing\n`EffectId as BridgeEffectId` and then calling `resolve(BridgeEffectId(id), ..)`\ntwenty lines from `resolve(EffectId::from_raw(id), ..)`. That alias is now gone.\n\nThe parked one is renamed rather than the bridge one because it is the newer of\nthe two (0.19.0, two months ago), `Registry` has exactly one user (`Parked`),\nno example references it, and it reaches only people running a custom FFI lane.\n`bridge::EffectId` is in all six example `ffi.rs` files and in every shell\nwrapper ever written against Crux. `ParkedEffectId` is also the name the code\nalready believed it had — `effect_id.rs` has always panicked with\n\"ParkedEffectId index overflow\".\n\nNothing crosses the FFI differently: `bridge::EffectId` is `#[serde(transparent)]`\nand `#[facet(transparent)]`, so generated Swift, Kotlin, TypeScript and C# see a\nplain `u32`. The only occurrence of \"EffectId\" in generated code is a doc comment\ncarried over from `Request`.","tree":{"sha":"e0933de2946300b38dbc59ff41fcd324519e9fca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/e0933de2946300b38dbc59ff41fcd324519e9fca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/f678527d42048d893eabd07d0e757f0f0bd4792b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","receive