"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/83e5717cf9c8fee722bcd4872ca113963c46cf5f"}],"sha":"cdb465e212635a790ee21c08e6e08d3a7719851b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/cdb465e212635a790ee21c08e6e08d3a7719851b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/83e5717cf9c8fee722bcd4872ca113963c46cf5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T16:44:28Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T07:21:08Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"refactor(http)!: HttpError::Http no longer has optional headers or body\n\nResponse::new is now the variant''s only constructor, and it always\nsupplies both, so the Options described states that could not occur.\nTightening them costs downstream nothing: the variant is\n#[non_exhaustive], so it cannot be constructed outside the crate, and\nthe accessors still return Option because the other variants have\nneither headers nor a body.\n\nheaders() therefore has a simpler contract - None means \"not a\nrejection\" rather than \"a rejection with nothing to describe it\" - and\nbody() no longer has to distinguish None from Some(vec![]).\n\nSize is unchanged at 72 bytes: Box and Vec are both niche-optimised, so\nthe Options were free at runtime and misleading in the API.","tree":{"sha":"5d41306f1d905ef64110f552aa36911e2dcce543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/5d41306f1d905ef64110f552aa36911e2dcce543"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/83e5717cf9c8fee722bcd4872ca113963c46cf5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/83e5717cf9c8fee722bcd4872ca113963c46cf5f","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDgzZTU3MTdjZjljOGZlZTcyMmJjZDQ4NzJjYTExMzk2M2M0NmNmNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca","sha":"9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca"}],"sha":"83e5717cf9c8fee722bcd4872ca113963c46cf5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/83e5717cf9c8fee722bcd4872ca113963c46cf5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T16:30:04Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T07:21:08Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"feat(http)!: remove From<http_types::Error> for HttpError\n\nThe impl mapped an http-types middleware error onto HttpError::Http,\nwhich now means only a server rejection. Nothing in the crate consumes\nit - compat.rs converts Request and Response, not Error - so this is a\npublic-surface removal under the optional http-types feature.\n\nIt is not rehomed onto a new variant because the http-types feature is\nslated for removal in full: http is the only HTTP type system crux_http\nwill keep. The rest of the feature (mod compat, the pub use http_types\nre-export) comes out in its own change.","tree":{"sha":"f1730ffdfeff162491b45a463f7c987e2938dbc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/f1730ffdfeff162491b45a463f7c987e2938dbc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca","node_id":"C_kwDOIKc9NtoAKDllNTFlMDEwNGMyYWQ3ODYyNjg1NmJhMDg2OGMyMDJlNmZhZWMzY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/redbadger/crux/commit/4bd0d6b0fade6749d339703a1c76ad0a4c466152","sha":"4bd0d6b0fade6749d339703a1c76ad0a4c466152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/4bd0d6b0fade6749d339703a1c76ad0a4c466152"}],"sha":"9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/9e51e0104c2ad78626856ba0868c202e6faec3ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/4bd0d6b0fade6749d339703a1c76ad0a4c466152/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T16:26:08Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T07:21:08Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"feat(http)!: split non-rejection errors out of HttpError::Http\n\nHttpError::Http is documented as \"the server answered with a 4xx or 5xx\",\nbut two other things constructed it, and since headers were added they\npresented as fully-formed rejections:\n\n- Response::body_bytes reported an already-taken body as an Http error\n  carrying the *successful* response''s status and headers, so code()\n  could return Some(200).\n- RawResponse::try_from reported a status outside 100-999 as a rejection\n  with that code.\n\nBoth now have variants of their own, BodyAlreadyTaken and\nInvalidStatusCode(u16), so Http means only a server rejection and\ncode() is Some if and only if the request was rejected.\n\nBodyAlreadyTaken carries nothing: the caller holds the Response, so the\nstatus and headers it used to report were already in hand - and described\na successful response, which is what made them misleading.\n\nThe enum is deliberately left exhaustive. Adding a variant stays a\nbreaking change so that an app mapping HttpError onto its own error type\ngets a compile error naming the new failure mode.","tree":{"sha":"8356e5f4ebcf6278fedc2161139ad8fb304eb29a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/8356e5f4ebcf6278fedc2161139ad8fb304eb29a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/4bd0d6b0fade6749d339703a1c76ad0a4c466152","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/StuartHarris","id":203552,"login":"StuartHarris","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzU1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https: