uartHarris/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/commits/731c47cb939fc4ab8aa21bb8323f8fb0b0b51c2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T13:52:09Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T14:03:12Z","email":"stuart.harris@red-badger.com","name":"Stuart Harris"},"message":"refactor(examples): align the remaining shells with the union port\n\ncounter-routing had drifted from the other shells: it wrapped the\ngenerated `serializeHttpResult` / `serializeSseResponse` in pass-through\nhelpers, passed an explicit type argument to `matchEffect`, and left its\nasync IIFEs unmarked. Call the generated helpers directly and use the\nsame `(e): void =>` arms and `void` prefix as counter-http, so the four\ncounter shells read identically.\n\nweather''s kv handler wrapped every arm in `Promise.resolve`, but all five\nare synchronous — the `async` signature already wraps the result.","tree":{"sha":"7cf3b39e87b2f87f20717fe55c8c61bbb927a4eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/trees/7cf3b39e87b2f87f20717fe55c8c61bbb927a4eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redbadger/crux/git/commits/731c47cb939fc4ab8aa21bb8323f8fb0b0b51c2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203552?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StuartHarris/gists