m/users/OmarIthawi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-atlas/commits/e407f8f257296119014721ea5f9aaf18d67fe799/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-04-08T07:36:41Z","email":"i@omardo.com","name":"Omar Al-Ithawi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-04-08T07:36:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Allow pulling translations from a commit hash (#62)\n\n* feat: Allow pulling translations from a commit hash\n\nBy switching from clone to an explicit init+fetch we can get better control\nof what commits are fetched. clone only allows targeting a branch or a\ntag, but fetch can ask for any commit. The caveat is that the server needs\nto allow this via `uploadpack.allowReachableSHA1InWant` and similar.\n\nMinor changes:\n\n- checkout is now also quiet by default\n\nSee https://github.com/openedx/openedx-atlas/issues/48\n\n* chore: run make gengetoptions\n\n* feat: print atlas pull total disk usage for testing purposes\n\n* feat: add tests for bandwidth and disk usage\n\n* chore: run make gengetoptions with v3.3.2\n\n* feat: disable bandwidth calculations on Mac\n\njust in case if it''s not compatible\n\n* fix: use actual size, without rouning up to the closest 512\n\n* fix: upgrade github actions to macos-13 to avoid stalling\n\nalso updated ubuntu and other actions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Tim McCormack <tmccormack@edx.org>","tree":{"sha":"434a5086483e1ead591075810bb372da27304acc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-atlas/git/trees/434a5086483e1ead591075810bb372da27304acc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-atlas/git/commits/e407f8f257296119014721ea5f9aaf18d67fe799","verification":{"payload":"tree 434a5086483e1ead591075810bb372da27304acc\nparent 9ea96b69d799dd75aa5a9057c9d74043cdecf5e9\nauthor Omar Al-Ithawi <i@omardo.com> 1744097801 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1744097801 +0300\n\nfeat: Allow pulling translations from a commit hash (#62)\n\n* feat: Allow pulling translations from a commit hash\n\nBy switching from clone to an explicit init+fetch we can get better control\nof what commits are fetched. clone only allows targeting a branch or a\ntag, but fetch can ask for any commit. The caveat is that the server needs\nto allow this via `uploadpack.allowReachableSHA1InWant` and similar.\n\nMinor changes:\n\n- checkout is now also quiet by default\n\nSee https://github.com/openedx/openedx-atlas/issues/48\n\n* chore: run make gengetoptions\n\n* feat: print atlas pull total disk usage for testing purposes\n\n* feat: add tests for bandwidth and disk usage\n\n* chore: run make gengetoptions with v3.3.2\n\n* feat: disable bandwidth calculations on Mac\n\njust in case if it''s not compatible\n\n* fix: use actual size, without rouning up to the closest 512\n\n* fix: upgrade github actions to macos-13 to avoid stalling\n\nalso updated ubuntu and other actions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Tim McCormack <tmccormack@edx.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJn9NIJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1Z0QAHBCRs5Mirvk01CjofLWDS/f\nmb+jvWKY/Xtd/rp8NdCQ822Lpp1oafGveK9r6Wc/UOqnQaoj1P4itV1x4zQuwA5E\nWRAbtcjQxkYgyYoNV5JPCgpvcDK7CdiS4bXTZ/UjgMfhUtOCIwRvN/HqRcPjaB+T\npnGSoUcvz51yoR3n2DM052vXlUf5QdQFD9GntvJuKI9vrr72YfP8b7w7jiMUz0wx\npShu8GVYltG65YV7/kRB9qi9hbiEQ7afdG97Otw8N2rnvv9DbrtHEeesZLv5pM0Q\n9KKw5xQXGGDZWtgh2Ud3lcCK1a/H3Ht8I/fBJvv/1alE2PoDZZRANlkjxk3LZe0t\nMWc8BI6M/1U7Mp6lCsEJ9aUsrHZoCRSQbTPZcF89kWpOQStjFrB9s1k3jpYIUBNW\nabLKIURFSHB10i35QXWY8Vr1jzClh3NQPcVW/RKzRWwTqLw1y6hbBOM+N7dnjW2M\nhMlXJpFmDSzbWpYATLdrWETaWe+m97jzfU2kOxPLa4qyZn8Y6dOIa66wkrQ3h+kZ\nUAazDR8TAykcnaHK11ESQrUZojXDyL7inlZCjUUZq/iI66iBlCevGS/Li1Nj58Hd\nuWafbvbR/YUMHVvgsUKMqi8ozkn+JutI0oebp3zqMYq5fGBnVkZo08KpPnidIgGB\n2lryEEpxI6hVgkZjW1xV\n=8M3h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-04-08T07:38:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4",